ase confirm how long that process is expected to take? Please let us know if there is anything else we can do to facilitate or expedite the necessary approvals at this stage.&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;PG&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorFrom: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 06 November 2025 15:43To: Nick Paolazzi &lt;npaolazzi@gramercy.com&gt;Cc: Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: FW: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation - Toremis&nbsp;Hi Nick &nbsp;We have received some further queries from our brokers regarding the proposed topup to the Nox policies (+£17m LOI)&nbsp;They want a call tomorrow to discuss 1b, would it be possible to discuss with you on a quick call before hand?&nbsp;Query from insurer below, let me know if you are available &nbsp;TomOn the economics - we will review the existing cross-collateralisation arrangements with a view to how they might be adapted for our purposes. We do have two requests on this side of things though:We note that for the existing arrangements, PG is the only claimant-side party. Our current view is that we would also want Gramercy as a party, either in its own right or as a guarantor. Is this acceptable to PG/Gramercy?On a related point, we would like to better understand how any settlement proceeds would flow through the existing waterfall(s), including the arrangements with cash flow up to Gramercy. Essentially, we would like to be able to understand what the effect of, for example, a settlement with Mercedes, would have on the money flowing through the waterfall in order to assess the extent to which such a settlement would then protect us from adverse results against other defendants. It would also be useful to be able to see the effect of varying levels of settlement. We assume that PG has excel 