ed to other members of staff who have been required to take a period of sickness during their notice period?&nbsp;&nbsp;Regarding my final pay, and in the event I am entitled to receive full pay for my absence (subject to the above), I believe my final pay should consist of:&nbsp;Full pay from 1 December to 12 December (anticipated as full pay under 13.4 of my contract)Any full pay for days which I return to full work;Outstanding annual leave of 6 days; and11 days worth of my acting up allowance (£3,175 gross). The 1 September letter from Raminder confirms that this will be effective from 1 September 2025 and will be reviewed on a monthly basis. It further states that any changes to this will be discussed in advance and confirmed in writing. I have received no such notice and so this is still due paid for this month.&nbsp;&nbsp;In terms of the company equipment:&nbsp;I note my account has been disabled on account of allowing me to focus on my health and recovery, thank you for this. I do note however that this will prevent me from progressing or completing any handover before 15 December. This will constrict the time I am available to complete this in.&nbsp;Thank you for confirming a courier can be arranged. If a courier can be arranged to attend my property on the afternoon of Friday 12 December 2025, I will have the computer screens and spare laptop ready to be collected.Noted regarding the £1,000 being withheld. Can you please confirm that this will not be unreasonably withheld, i.e. in circumstances where the courier has collected the equipment on 12 December, but it is not delivered to Pogust Goodhead by 15 December?&nbsp;Thank you for providing the TELUS information, I will likely avail of this while it is available.&nbsp;&nbsp;I look forward to hearing from you with confirmation of the above.&nbsp;&nbsp;Best wishes,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Natasha Geraldo Baird &lt;ngeraldobaird@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;01 December 2025 12:48To:&nbsp;