&nbsp;


The &quot;why&quot; obviously needs to be completed by those more in the know; when we agree the template we can send it to them.&nbsp; Anna, for what it is worth, in my experience
 of the committees I think the more reasons we give, the less likely they are to request a call, and there is some urgency to the email.


&nbsp;


We have a duty to our clients to send the email, I believe, so this needs to go fairly quickly.&nbsp; In Michael's case it might be more even urgent, since the Defendants
 know of his resignation: there is a risk that his resignation will go public, and it would be best for the committee relationships if they found out from us.


