Matt


&nbsp;


&nbsp;


____________________________________________


&nbsp;


Dear [Case] Claimant Committee,


&nbsp;


We write with an important update on your case and request for instructions.&nbsp; We should inform you in advance that there is no intention for this to imperil the
 success of the case.


&nbsp;


Update


&nbsp;


First, with regret I have resigned from my position as [X] at Pogust Goodhead.&nbsp; I can confirm that my reasons have nothing
 to do with the merits of the case: the Claimants' skeleton argument was served on 18 September 2025 and we are confident in its strength.&nbsp; We look forward to holding the Defendants to account, and I will continue to work on the case for as long as I am able.


&nbsp;


Request for instructions


&nbsp;


Second, Pogust Goodhead intends to step away from its role as &quot;Lead Solicitor&quot; in the litigation.&nbsp; This is a Court-appointed role that formally entitles the firm
 to run the case on behalf of all Claimants, not just those who formally instruct this firm.&nbsp; We have done this because [...].&nbsp; Again, this has not been done with any intention to imperil the success of the case or impending
 trial.


&nbsp;


Please confirm by return that you agree to instruct Pogust Goodhead to apply to remove itself as Lead Solicitor for this case.


&nbsp;


If you would like a meeting to discuss the above request for instructions, we are of course happy to arrange a meeting with us and the board of the firm.


&nbsp;


Kind regards,


&nbsp;


[X]


