I a&nbsp;From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 03 November 2025 15:21To: Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Greg Lewis &lt;glewis@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Erika Saluzzo &lt;esaluzzo@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Fw: Ford Client Committee&nbsp;I've not looked at this - I'm on call with hospital so wont be looking at this for an hour at least.​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Monday, November 3, 2025 3:15 PMTo: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Ford Litigation Team &lt;fordteam@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Ford Client Committee &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks both. Anna - noted it was pre-approved but I'm just mindful of the directions I've been given hence asking for permission.&nbsp;&nbsp;As discussed, the draft that was sent to me is inaccurate in that it put all of the adverse costs under a single application, which was not correct. Similarly, it wasn't drafted with my previous communications with the Committee in mind. As such, and to account for those, the draft is below with my amends.&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;#######################################&nbsp;Dear Richard, Toby and Dinah,&nbsp;Claimant Committee,&nbsp;I hope you are all well.&nbsp;&nbsp;Further to the instructions from Toby and Dinah last week, I can confirm that Pogust Goodhead will engage with the Defendants in respect of their application to amend their Individual Defences, on the standard basis.&nbsp;&nbsp;The firm will keep you updated in respect of this and the final position of the costs, as we progress and the firm will confirm and seek your instructions on those costs at the appropriate juncture, including when it comes to finalising the total costs schedule, and in relation to any offers from the Defendants.&nbsp;&nbsp;With regard to the previous application made by the Defendants, which I advised you of in my update of 26 September (regarding our software expert report that was heard on 10 and 11 September), we are now in a position to confirm We write to update you on the costs position&nbsp;as it relates to that application&nbsp;for the Ford Litigation.&nbsp;case following the hearing that took place on 10 and 11 September 2025. This aspect of this update&nbsp;communication is being sent for your information only and requires no action from you.&nbsp;As previously advised in my updates on 8 and 26 September, the September hearing concerned&nbsp;each of&nbsp;the Defendants’ applications in respect of the automotive software engineering report, the report of Mr Juston Smithers, and the evidence of Professor Tate (climatology). For those applications, s&nbsp;that parts of the software engineering reports be struck out because they overlapped with portions of the mechanical engineering reports. T the judge agreed with some, but not all, of the applicants’ requests, including in respect of the automotive software report, and Mr Smither's report. As a result, the Court was most likely to make a ruling that the&nbsp;Claimants collectively, be required to make payment to the Defendants, for their costs of the application (as is generally the case when a party is successful in an application). The Defendants initially sought their costs on the indemnity basis, however we managed to negotiate with them in respect of those costs to reduce them to a total of cohort are now to pay a total of&nbsp;£182,865.10 to the Ford Defendants in respect of the legal costs to prepare those applications. The split of those costs between the applications was that £159,298.81 was in respect of the automotive software engineering report, and £23,566.29 was in respect of Mr Smithers report.&nbsp;&nbsp;The total share of costs to be borne by Pogust Goodhead clients is £90,134.19&nbsp;(the “PG Costs”).&nbsp;As you know, and under the terms of the conditional fee agreement that you and all other Claimants entered when instructing Pogust Goodhead, adverse costs insurance policies are in place for this litigation. These are referred to as After The Event insurance (&quot;ATE&quot;)., and t The ATE insurers have confirmed that the PG Costs will be paid in full by the insurers under these policies. There is therefore no amount payable by Pogust Goodhead clients in respect of these PG Costs.&nbsp;&nbsp;Funds have been received from the insurers to meet the PG Costs,&nbsp;and&nbsp;payment to the Defendants will therefore be made direct from the client account, today.&nbsp;To reassure you, the outcome of the September hearing has had no bearing on the merit of the Claimants’ case, which remains unchanged. We will write to you under separate cover next week with a summary about how the PDD trial is progressing.&nbsp;I will continue to provide you with updates on the progress of the trial. To remind you however, Ford commences next Monday, 10 November and should any of you wish to be provided with a link, or attend in person, please let me know. &nbsp;&nbsp;Yours sincerely,&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead Michael &amp; the Ford Litigation Team&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: 03 November 2025 3:01 PMTo: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Ford Litigation Team &lt;fordteam@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Ford Client Committee &nbsp;Hi Alicia,&nbsp;Thanks. I've just flagged to Anna that the update originally drafted was inaccurate so I am re-drafting. I will send it through to you both for approval.&nbsp;It will then need to be tailored for the other litigations.&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Michael​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344From: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: 03 November 2025 2:58 PMTo: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Ford Litigation Team &lt;fordteam@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Ford Client Committee &nbsp;Thanks Mike. Looks great. Loving your work!&nbsp;A​​​​Alicia&nbsp;AliniaChief&nbsp;Executive&nbsp;Officer+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;629From: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Monday, November 3, 2025 2:42 PMTo: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Ford Litigation Team &lt;fordteam@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Re: Ford Client Committee &nbsp;Hi Michael&nbsp;Thank you - those were pre-approved so subject to any tweaks you feel are required, all good.&nbsp;ThanksAnna​​​​Anna&nbsp;VargaPartner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7890&nbsp;043&nbsp;699From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent: Monday, November 3, 2025 2:35 PMTo: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Ford Litigation Team &lt;fordteam@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Ford Client Committee &nbsp;Dear both,&nbsp;I hope you are well.&nbsp;&nbsp;I am writing to seek permission to write to the Ford Claimant Committee.&nbsp;Communications have been going out to various Committees today on payments made in respect of adverse costs.&nbsp;&nbsp;Can you please grant permission for me to liaise with the Claimant Committee?&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Michael&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Michael&nbsp;Burke(He/Him)Partner+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7960&nbsp;032&nbsp;34407960&nbsp;032&nbsp;344&nbsp;"}

