ints from the CMH2 judgment. It follows broadly the same structure as last year’s note following CMH1.&nbsp;I have not yet had a chance to discuss the final section (in relation to ATE cover) with Ben, and it’s a point on which there could be different views, so I would be grateful if this could be treated as a draft and not circulated more widely just yet. But I wanted to get it to you so that you could review and identify if there were any other queries about the judgment which you consider it would be helpful to address.&nbsp;Best wishes,Simon&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Simon Teasdale &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;30 September 2025 17:42To:&nbsp;Sophia Thomson &lt;SThomson@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Fiona Huddleston &lt;FHuddleston@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah Bingham &lt;sbingham@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Suzanna Popplewell &lt;spopplewell@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Jamie Macfarlane &lt;jmacfarlane@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; KLatham@kingschambers.com; Theo Barclay &lt;T.Barclay@4newsquare.com&gt;; Benjamin Williams KC &lt;B.Williams@4newsquare.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;Re: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Hi Sophia&nbsp;Apologies for the delay. I’m just on my way back from a hearing in Liverpool today but will aim to get a draft out to you tomorrow for an initial review (to make sure it covers the points you need etc).&nbsp;Thanks for the heads up on the disbursements query. I’ll cover this as best I can from a budgeting perspective, though I suspect in practice this may be more a point for the contribution agreements etc that George is across.&nbsp;ThanksSimon&nbsp;Sent from Outlook for iOSFrom:&nbsp;Sophia Thomson &lt;SThomson@leighday.co.uk&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Tuesday, September 30, 2025 11:01:35 AMTo:&nbsp;Fiona Huddleston &lt;FHuddleston@leighday.co.uk&gt;; Simon Teasdale &lt;S.Teasdale@4newsquare.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Sarah B