ollect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;03 December 2025 21:18To:&nbsp;Nick Paolazzi &lt;npaolazzi@gramercy.com&gt;; Joshua Katz &lt;jkatz@gramercy.com&gt;; Marc Zelina &lt;mzelina@gramercy.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;James Taylor &lt;JTaylor@gramercy.com&gt;; Josh O'Melia &lt;jomelia@gramercy.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation - Toremis&nbsp;Hi Nick.&nbsp;Can we say that the proceeds will be directed to “the applicable office account held by the Law Firm that has been secured to its funders as indicated in writing by the Law Firm”? That would be consistent with the definition of Funder Account and with the cash management system. It would also capture the Gramercy Collection Account (G1) to the extent that there are no other senior funders (i.e., Fulcrum, Locke) whose agreements require proceeds to be directed to a Funder Account in accordance with 5.9 of the Credit Agreement.&nbsp;Regarding the individual (non–cross-collateralised) priority deeds, your question is whether they follow the same payment instructions as in the overarching deed? They do not specify which of the law firm’s bank accounts should receive the proceeds payable to the law firm. The current amendments to the individual deeds only amend the parties (update barristers under CFAs and the new insurer), and the insurance layer that is being added to the waterfall. I’m afraid we cannot make any substantive amendments at this stage, given that the previous insurers (Litica, Vale, and Ignite) approved these documents quite some time ago.&nbsp;In case you need, the full original individual deeds were shared with Gramercy previously in this link &nbsp;Emissions&nbsp;Kind regards&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2000. A list of partners is available on our website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our Privacy Policy.From:&nbsp;Nick Paolazzi &lt;npaolazzi@gramercy.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;03 December 2025 20:22To:&nbsp;Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joshua Katz &lt;jkatz@gramercy.com&gt;; Marc Zelina &lt;mzelina@gramercy.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;James Taylor &lt;JTaylor@gramercy.com&gt;; Josh O'Melia &lt;jomelia@gramercy.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation - Toremis&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Carolina – we reviewed and have just one comment.&nbsp; When the funds are released from the Insurer Distribution Account, could they be directed to the Gramercy Collections Account (for G1) instead of the law firm?&nbsp; Also, we reviewed the Priorities Deed sent at 7:31AM ET this morning.&nbsp; Do the individual priorities deeds follow the same form?Thanks,Nick&nbsp;From:&nbsp;Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, December 3, 2025 7:31 AMTo:&nbsp;Nick Paolazzi &lt;npaolazzi@gramercy.com&gt;; Joshua Katz &lt;jkatz@gramercy.com&gt;; Marc Zelina &lt;mzelina@gramercy.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;James Taylor &lt;JTaylor@gramercy.com&gt;; Josh O'Melia &lt;jomelia@gramercy.com&gt;; Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Donatas Juskauskas &lt;djuskauskas@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Enquiry for Additional ATE Cover – Pan-NOx Emissions Litigation - ToremisImportance:&nbsp;High&nbsp;[External Email]Nick, Josh, Marc,&nbsp;Following our discussion yesterday, please find attached the latest version signed off by Toremis.&nbsp;Please let us know if you have any comments, and confirm that Gramercy will sign the acknowledgment wording per the attached.&nbsp;Again, we kindly ask you to prioritise this today as we need to submit signed versions to Toremis and get their confirmation of cover ahead of our court deadline this Friday.&nbsp;Thank you.&nbsp;Kind regards&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. 