Hi Anna, all &nbsp;To the extent the broader letter to the Defendants doesn&#8217;t go before 4pm, please see below a suggested short response to Renault&#8217;s request for information ahead of the 4pm deadline this afternoon. &nbsp;BestJess&nbsp;***********************************&nbsp;Dear Sirs/Madams, &nbsp;We acknowledge receipt of Renault&#8217;s request for information regarding the individual within Pogust Goodhead has assumed overall responsibility for the Emissions litigation.&nbsp;We confirm that we propose to share an update with the Defendant firms addressing this point in advance of the stated deadline of noon on 25 September 2025. &nbsp;On this basis, we confirm that there is no need for Renault to issue the application notice. &nbsp;&nbsp;Yours faithfully &nbsp;Pogust Goodhead&nbsp;From: SL-UKRenault &lt;SL-UKRenault@signaturelitigation.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 11:34To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Pan Nox Emissions &lt;PanNoxEmissions@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; HSF NOx Litigation &lt;hsfnoxlitigation@hsfkramer.com&gt;; MW-Ford UK Emissions &lt;mwfordukemissions@mcguirewoods.com&gt;; Team-PCD-CGSHOnly &lt;team-pcd-cgshonly@cgsh.com&gt;; Nissan Litigation HL &lt;nissanhluk@hoganlovells.com&gt;; Nissan Renault Leighday &lt;NissanRenault@leighday.co.uk&gt;; SL-UKRenault &lt;SL-UKRenault@signaturelitigation.com&gt;Subject: Renault NOx Emissions Group Litigation [SIG-LIT-LIT.FID5824]&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Dear Sirs/Madams,&nbsp;We refer to our letters of 10 and 15 September 2025 and your letter dated 23 September 2025 received at 9.12pm (that letter asked us to provide related correspondence to Ms Alinia or Mr Morris).&nbsp;Renault is continuing to consider your letter and notes that your firm has not confirmed who is the partner/are the partners of your firm with direct, and SRA, responsibility for the Pan-NOx litigation.&nbsp; Accordingly, in the short time available since receiving your letter, Renault has prepared the attached draft application notice and draft order seeking this information.&nbsp; It is reasonable to assume that your firm already knows without needing to investigate further who is running this litigation.&nbsp; The application therefore should not be necessary if your firm confirms it will provide the information sought in the attached draft application notice and draft order.&nbsp; Please confirm by 4pm today whether Pogust Goodhead is willing to provide this information by noon on 30 September 2025. &nbsp;This is a focused and specific point that Renault intends to have addressed at PTR2 if the Claimants do not provide such confirmation.&nbsp; Whilst we appreciate this provides the Claimants with a short amount of time today to confirm if an application does not need to be issued, Renault is willing to provide the Claimants until 30 September to confirm the information. &nbsp;Yours faithfully, &nbsp;T:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;20&nbsp;3818&nbsp;3500&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Signature Litigation LLP is a limited liability partnership registered in England and Wales with registered number OC371068 and is authorised and regulated by the Solicitors Regulation Authority with SRA ID 567257. A list of names of the members of the LLP are available for inspection at the firm&#8217;s registered address at 138 Fetter Lane, London, EC4A 1BT. The word &quot;partner&quot; denotes an LLP member, or a consultant or employee with equivalent standing and qualifications. Further regulatory information can be found in the Legal Notices which appear on our website at https://www.signaturelitigation.com/legal/.This email (and any attachments) is confidential and may also be legally privileged and is intended solely for the use of the individual or entity addressed above. If you are not the intended recipient, please immediately notify the sender, then delete it from your system. You should not copy it or use it for any purpose, nor disclose its contents to any other person.Although we have taken reasonable precautions to ensure that no viruses are present in this email and any attachments, you should also ensure that this email and any attachments are virus-free before opening as we cannot accept responsibility for any loss or damage arising from their use. Please also note that emails sent or received may be monitored to ensure compliance with the law and with our policies.We will never use email to notify you of a change to any bank account details we have already provided to you. If you receive any email purporting to come from this firm which seeks to do this, please contact us immediately by telephone and do not act on it or reply to it. We cannot accept responsibility for any loss if you do not follow these instructions."}

