Hi Neil &nbsp;There are tweaks to %s &nbsp;From: Neil Pigott &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt; Sent: 10 October 2025 14:24To: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Carolina,&nbsp;Alicia’s Witness Statement referred to Gramercy LLC and so at this stage for consistency with that and to avoid opening up questions it would be best to leave that as is, I am afraid.&nbsp;The addition of “or costs” is fine.&nbsp;We are looking over the updated draft now, for which thanks.&nbsp;Neil&nbsp;Neil&nbsp;Pigott​​​​PartnerT:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;20&nbsp;4574&nbsp;1005|M:&nbsp;+44&nbsp;75&nbsp;5741&nbsp;2828E:&nbsp;&nbsp;neil.pigott@pallasllp.com110&nbsp;Bishopsgate,&nbsp;London,&nbsp;EC2N&nbsp;4AYpallasllp.com&nbsp;|&nbsp;LinkedInFrom: Carolina Koschdoski de Souza &lt;csouza@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 10 October 2025 13:54To: Neil Pigott &lt;Neil.Pigott@pallasllp.com&gt;; Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Tom Crow &lt;tcrow@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jessica Fechner &lt;jfechner@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Dilan Alma &lt;dalma@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Defendants’ Submissions and Draft Order – Costs of CMH2&nbsp;Neil,&nbsp;Can we please take out the below? Gramercy LLC refers to the asset management entity as opposed to the investment funds, which are the parties to the funding agreements. My point is that Gramercy is averse to including the asset management company.&nbsp;The information above is given without prejudice to any position that Gramercy LLC may wish to take should it be met with an application by your clients.&nbsp;I am unsure about the word in red below, but I believe that the explanation is in the following para copied below. Therefore, although the facility is repaid from proceeds that PG recovers as profit costs from the cases, the money characterization has become income when PG repays the facility. Do you agree?&nbsp;There is also no element of return under either facility relating to a share of damages or costs recovered by the clients in the proceedings.&nbsp;Gramercy 1 and Gramercy 3 have rights to repayment toward any outstanding facility amounts via sweep mechanisms set out in the loan agreements of all income received by Pogust Goodhead, which obviously includes income that results from cases successfully litigated under CFAs. This is a right to repayment of the facility and does not represent a share of any recovery by the clients in the proceedings.&nbsp;Thank you.&nbsp;Kind regards &nbsp;​​​​Carolina&nbsp;Koschdoski&nbsp;de&nbsp;SouzaLegal&nbsp;DirectorThis email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the