Dear Board, Anna,

&nbsp;

We have been sent a copy of the draft Agency Agreement by LD late last night and we are considering this. As an initial point, the definition of &quot;Common Work&quot; is not wide
 enough to capture all common work. It is currently a vague halfway house that doesn't offer clarity or certainty, and we suspect will further encourage the Defendants (and other interested parties) to complain and/or ask more questions.

&nbsp;

In addition, we cannot stress enough how traumatic we and the entire team are finding this process, and that it is happening on the eve of trial. That is exacerbated by the
 fact that we are only properly notified of proposed fundamental changes to our employment through Martyn Day and his team, who as a third party, is not our employer, and where it appears to us these changes are being pushed through as a fait accompli publicly,
 yet without the case leads consultation and agreement.&nbsp;It is massively unfair on each of us, it is not creating a good working environment and may prejudice our ability to produce the level of work required for this trial.&nbsp;&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Before we are in a position to give our agreement (which for the avoidance of doubt we consider necessary, as with all named personnel, before the agreement is capable of
 execution), we have a number of points that require clarification:

&nbsp;

·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
we be provided sight of the advice from Ben Williams KC (and any other applicable counsel) who have advised on the AA;

·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
before the agreement is consented to (at least by the case leads) that there is an agreed and defined role for Pete Gallagher in the individual
 and pan-NOx litigations, documented (and signed) alongside the AA;

·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
how the claimant committees, and wider claimant cohort, will be informed that the teams with conduct of their cases are under dual supervision of
 Martyn Day, and Alicia Alina, in respect of the different spheres of work (common / generic); and

·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
A &quot;step back&quot; clause is included such as to allow the case leads or team to step back from the AA if the personnel consider their regulatory / professional
 obligations are untenable with instructions given to them.

&nbsp;We also note that the intended agreement covers a list of PG personnel wider than just the case leads (the list provided by LD to Michael Burke at 8.23PM last night has
