n our&nbsp;website.&nbsp;For details about what personal information we collect and why, please see our&nbsp;Privacy Policy.From: Alicia Alinia Sent: 25 September 2025 16:29To: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: RE: Signature Application - Action required&nbsp;Hi Mike, &nbsp;Thanks for your email. &nbsp;We’ll consider all the points you’ve raised and revert as soon as possible. Anna will be responding on the specific points as they relate to the correspondence from Renault.&nbsp;ThanksA&nbsp;From: Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt; Sent: 25 September 2025 14:24To: Alicia Alinia &lt;aalinia@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Howard Morris &lt;hmorris@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Joseph Moreno &lt;jmoreno@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Anna Varga &lt;avarga@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Cc: Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject: Signature Application - Action requiredImportance: High&nbsp;Dear Board,&nbsp;In follow up to my email at 12.52 today, I am writing to ask for immediate attention to be given to addressing my (and the other case leaves) employment position to the Defendants, Court, clients and any other relevant stake holders.&nbsp;As Signature's draft application points out at 8(b)(iii) - a letter was sent out yesterday, naming me as the PG contact.&nbsp;&nbsp;That I am named as the contact appears to have been an administrative oversight, and I put no blame on the sender of the letter, however this has now lead to a misleading position, or what will be a mislead position if not immediately clarified, underpinning the concerns I had regarding paragraph 27 of the letter sent to the Defendants on Tuesday 23 September (see my email at 12.52 today and my suggestion at 15.59 on 23 September).&nbsp;&nbsp;The SRA Co