&nbsp;
The Defendants have made it clear that should the parties be unable to reach an agreement, they will be seeking the Court make an order of indemnity costs against the Claimants
 at the PTR on Monday 6 October. The approach taken by so far has been to sound out the Defendants as to whether we can reach an agreement that avoids them making such an application. LD have sent a WP offer to Mercedes, &quot;offer[ing] either (i) 66% in relation
 to your clients’ statement of costs in respect of the Dr Heitz application, payable within 28 days, or (ii) an interim payment of your indemnity costs of 50% now, payable within 28 days, with the remainder to be assessed.&quot;
&nbsp;
We do not think this is something that will be acceptable across all of the Defendants, not least because there are nuances to how &quot;successful&quot; each Defendant was in their
 application.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
We would like to request authority to go to 80% of the due costs of the Heitz reports, 80% of the costs of the Smithers costs, 80% of the Glow Plugs costs, and for us to push
