&nbsp;
The applications (and costs pursuant to those applications) as they relate to the reports of Dr Tate and Mr Smithers, we are seeking be pushed off
 and be costs in the case. The Defendants were not wholly successful in those applications. We think we will be able to agree this with the Defendants.
&nbsp;
In respect of the applications as they relate to Dr Heitz however, we have significant concerns that if we are unable to reach an agreement with the
 Defendants, and they make an application to the Court, they will be awarded costs on an indemnity basis. We are today meeting on a Without Prejudice basis with the Defendants to seek to find agreement with them in respect of costs.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
To make it clear - PG is not and will never be responsible for 100% of these costs, only their proportionate share as per the number of claimants on
 the group register in each litigation.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
For the avoidance of doubt, as a result of the information being struck out from Dr Heitz's reports, we do not consider that there has been an adverse
 impact on the merits of the case.&nbsp;
&nbsp;
Helena will be in touch to arrange a meeting later this week to discuss this, and the wider case, in more detail. We will also provide you with a further
 update once we have spoken to the Defendants.&nbsp;
