&nbsp;
We are currently in the process of renewing your practising certificates. Pogust Goodhead can perform a bulk renewal of these practising certificates, but each individual solicitor must
‘opt in’ to the bulk renewal on the SRA website portal.
&nbsp;
Statement of competence
As part of this exercise, each solicitor qualified in England and Wales, and any registered European Lawyers are expected to make a declaration to the SRA confirming that they have reflected on the quality of their practice and addressed
 any learning needs in the past year. For further information please see SRA
 Competence Statement which sets out core standards all solicitors should be able to undertake competently.&nbsp;

&nbsp;
How to provide your declaration 
&nbsp;
Pogust Goodhead will be making a declaration to the SRA on your behalf as part of the bulk renewal. Once you have considered the competency statement, please complete the
Internal
 Declaration. 
&nbsp;
As part of the process, you may also upload evidence using the same link Internal Declaration and the attached template – whilst this step is not mandatory, you are encouraged to do so to help you maintain a record of your continuing professional
 development. 
&nbsp;
Please complete this by Close of Business on Friday 17th October.
&nbsp;
Opting In
Most people have already opted into the bulk renewal. If you have not done so, and you wish to be included in the process, please click the link below and select ‘opt in to bulk renewal’.&nbsp; Please ensure you opt in by the deadline of
Friday 17th October.
