f your indemnity costs of 50% now, payable within 28 days, with the remainder to be assessed.&quot;&nbsp;We do not think this is something that will be acceptable across all of the Defendants, not least because there are nuances to how &quot;successful&quot; each Defendant was in their application.&nbsp;&nbsp;We would like to request authority to go to 80% of the due costs of the Heitz reports, 80% of the costs of the Smithers costs, 80% of the Glow Plugs costs, and for us to push the Tate costs to be Costs in the Case. This would equate to:&nbsp;ReportMercedesRenaultNissanFordTotalHeitz£93,758.64£44,372.78£138,368.65£83,752.94£360,253.01Tate&nbsp;Smithers&nbsp;£8,428.79&nbsp;£12,390.22£20,819.01Glow Plugs&nbsp;£91,577.54£103,649.30&nbsp;TOTAL£93,758.64£144,379.11£242,017.95£96,143.16£576,298.86&nbsp;If we can be of any further assistance, please let us know.&nbsp;&nbsp;Thanks,&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead&nbsp;From:&nbsp;James Burke &lt;james.burke2@wtwco.com&gt;Sent:&nbsp;Wednesday, October 01, 2025 6:28 PMTo:&nbsp;Helena Yearwood &lt;hyearwood@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Michael Burke &lt;mburke@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;; Jonathan Simon &lt;Jonathan.Simon@wtwco.com&gt;Cc:&nbsp;Emissions Case Leads &lt;EmissionsCaseLeads@pogustgoodhead.com&gt;Subject:&nbsp;RE: Pan NOx Notification&nbsp;CAUTION: This email originated from outside of the organization. Do not click links or open attachments unless you recognize the sender and know the content is safe.&nbsp;Hi Helena,&nbsp;Apologies for missing your calls, I was in a meeting this afternoon.&nbsp;For the moment insurers have reserved their rights in respect of any claim on the policy. They have also asked whether PG previously informed insurers about these applications and/or sought consent to contest them?&nbsp;Would you be able to give more information about the timing and making of the applications, the decision to contest them and their notice to insurers? I can see that there have been references to the expert reports in the periodic NOx updates but no express mention of the Defendants’ applications.&nbsp;The i.) Mercedes, and ii.) NOx wrapper policies have slightly different exclusion clauses in relation to adverse costs attributable to interim applications.&nbsp;The Mercedes policy excludes any claim under the policy attributable to “any interim application made or resisted without Insurer’s Approval” (clause 2.1.4).&nbsp;The NOx wrapper policies (Ford, RN and CP) excludes, unless Insurers Approval has been given, any claim under the policy attributable to:“The Insured’s intention to apply for summary judgment under CPR Part 24 or to make any other application which will be listed for or take half a day or more” (clause 4.1.4)&nbsp;The insurers have not yet sought to rely on these clauses but I would imagine these clauses are the context in which they seek further information. Given clause 4.1.4 above, it may also be that a notification was not required under the policy in any event.&nbsp;Regarding your instructions to Counsel – can you let us know the offer to settle the matters that you would like us to put to insurers for their agreement?&nbsp;Kind regards,&nbsp;James Burke&nbsp;Associate Director (Solicitor)Litigation and Contingent Risk FINEX Global&nbsp;WTWOn behalf of Willis Limited, 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ (registered number 181116)On behalf of Willis Towers Watson SA/NV, Quai des Vennes, 4020, Liège, Belgium (registered as a branch in the UK at 51 Lime Street, London, EC3M 7DQ UK Branch Number BR021056) in relation to all EEA-regulated business&nbsp;D: +44 (0)20 31248037M: +44 (0)7831 162591&nbsp;james.burke2@wtwco.comwww.wtwco.com&nbsp;Financial, Professional, and Executive Risks (FINEX)Your Trusted Partner in Managing Complex Risk: Expertly navigating Litigation Risk, Cyber, Directors &amp; Officers, Financial Institutions, Mergers &amp; Acquisitions, Professional Indemnity, and Operational Risks within WTW.Part of our wider risk solutions capabilities at WTW&nbsp;At 