ndants’ claimed budgeted costs; and100% of approved future costs to Spring 2026.Given the level of incurred costs&nbsp;and the criticisms between Defendants regarding their figures, we consider that the sufficiency calculation can be revised downwards without materially affecting the adequacy of coverage. We propose the following revised basis:50% of the Defendants’ claimed incurred costs;50% of the Defendants’ claimed budgeted costs; and100% of approved future costs to 31 July 2026.On this revised basis, the following GLOs fall below the proposed coverage threshold:&nbsp;Mercedes&nbsp;-£953,580.35Ford-£838,961.27Renault-Nissan-£2,535,219.93PCD-£149,635.79Toyota-£136,927.40&nbsp;We would be grateful for your confirmation on whether additional excess layer coverage can be secured for these cases, specifically for&nbsp;Mercedes, Ford, and Renault-Nissan.We look forward to hearing from you as soon as possible.Kind regards,&nbsp;&nbsp;​​​​Sarah&nbsp;BinghamLegal&nbsp;Director+44&nbsp;(0)&nbsp;7484&nbsp;085&nbsp;187This email and any attachments are confidential and may also be privileged. If you receive this message in error, please contact the sender immediately, destroy the email and any attachments and do not use, copy, store or disclose this email and any attachments for any purpose. Pogust Goodhead does not accept service of documents by electronic means without express prior agreement.&nbsp;Pogust Goodhead is the trading name of&nbsp;PGMBM Law Ltd, a&nbsp;limited liability company registered in England and Wales (no. 6284764) with its&nbsp;registered office at&nbsp;53-64 Chancery House, Chancery Lane, London WC2A 1QS&nbsp;and authorised and regulated by the Solicitors' Regulation Authority. We use the term ‘partner’ to refer to an employee or consultant of Pogust Goodhead with equivalent standing or qualifications. No&nbsp;reference to a partner should be taken to imply partnership for the purposes of the Partnership Act 1890&nbsp;or Limited Liability Partnerships