Thank you for sharing the letter from Enyo in the IBRAM proceedings. We are preparing a draft, but would be very grateful for your input on the following questions before we share a more advanced draft with you:
&nbsp;


We understand from previous emails that Craig Shuttleworth is working on the matter. In a similar vein to our letter to Slaughter and May, we can explain that Craig is conducting / leading the proceedings,
 and you support him. Is that correct? Craig and Celine Barnwell have been involved since the beginning. Craig and I started working on the injunction on 22 February 2025 and then Celine took over - she and I worked together on
 this from mid-March and she increasingly took the lead as I was meant to move off onto Nox - for example by about late May, I had limited involvement. At the point of the Part 8 claim form which was issued on a protective basis, she was largely leading the
 matter, partly because there was a fair bit of client facing instructions that were needed and partly because I was meant to start pivoting away from BHP matters from April. &nbsp;Im fairly certain she put in a witness statement on this workstream. The irony is
 that the decision to initiate this injunction is something Craig and I strongly opposed but Tom G insisted on going ahead.



Are there any other partners that are / have been conducting the proceedings that we could mention?
